IMPORT prelude

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
--
-- The regulations count periods in three ways, and each is encoded as written (fork F1 in NOTES.md):
--   * "within 7 days after" a day (regs 21, 53, 56, 61, 92): the period starts the day after, so the last day is that
--     day plus 7 (Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(a), the day of the event excluded);
--   * "within 7 days beginning on" a day (reg 20(1)(b)) and "the day after the period of 120 [or 28] days beginning on"
--     a day (regs 19, 21(6), 22, 57(1)): the day itself is day 1, so 7 days beginning on day D end on D plus 6, and the
--     day after 120 days beginning on D is D plus 120;
--   * months and years ("within 3 months after", "a period of 12 months ending on", "once every 2 years"): the same day
--     number n months on, or the last day of that month where it has no such day.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The day n days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The number of days in a month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The day n calendar months after a day (n may be negative): the same day number n months on, or the last day of that
-- month where it has no such day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted from year 0` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted from year 0` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted from year 0` MODULO 12) PLUS 1

-- The day n years after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `years after` `the start` MEANS `the date` (n TIMES 12) `months after` `the start`

-- The first day of "the period of n months ending on" a day: the day after the same day n months earlier.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the` n `months ending on` `the last day` MEANS
    `the date` 1 `days after` (`the date` (0 MINUS n) `months after` `the last day`)
